  "notes": [
    "v3 used Langmuir (equilibrium adsorption) to describe a COVALENT, irreversible reaction. That spreads p_conj over 0.45-0.92 across sites and creates large one-arm leakage 2p(1-p) -- this is what destroyed the even-DAR preference, and no amount of parameter tuning could fix it.",
    "Maleimide-thiol is irreversible 2nd order: conversion = 1-exp(-k2*[P]*t). At k2=300.0 M^-1s^-1, [P]=60 uM, t=2.0 h the exponent is ~130, i.e. conversion ~1 in free solution. Site identity therefore gates ACCESS only, not chemistry.",
    "Free-solution conversion is capped at the empirically observed process yield CONJ_YIELD=0.96 (typical 0.92-0.98), because the protein surface microenvironment (desolvation, local steric, payload aggregation) lowers it below the ideal-solution value.",
    "Sensitivity over p_c = 0.50 -> 0.99 is included below; it shows even/odd is a steep, monotone function of conjugation conversion -- i.e. the even-DAR preference is a CONSEQUENCE of near-quantitative conjugation, not a fitted knob."
